Address Space Isolation, for LSF/MM/BPF 2024
============

This is a demo branch for the latest upstream version of ASI.

This represents a pretty minimal version of ASI, it importantly lacks
local-nonsensitive support and and any attempt to mitigate cross-SMT attacks, it
also only sandboxes KVM guests (not bare-metal userspace).

The branch itself is also a bit messy:

- Some code might look weird because it was taken from Google's internal branch
  where "easily-rebasable diff from upstream" is a goal. We'll need to look over
  the patches with this in mind before posting a PATCH (I guess it's not a big
  deal for an RFC).

- The commit history is messy and will contain redundant changes and reversions,
  plus commit messages are likely to miss important explanatory content.

Nonetheless it should be enough to illustrate how ASI works and lots of what you
can expect to see in future LKML posts.

